Falsifies `jh7110_pci_express::verification::outbound_window_accepts_every_power_of_two_size`.

The defect: the smallest window, one 4 KiB granule, is refused, so a tree that names a 4 KiB
range gets no translation entry at all.

Expected to fail: the harness's assertion that every power of two from 4 KiB up is accepted.

diff --git a/crates/jh7110_pci_express/src/bridge.rs b/crates/jh7110_pci_express/src/bridge.rs
index 1723209a6..923be3403 100644
--- a/crates/jh7110_pci_express/src/bridge.rs
+++ b/crates/jh7110_pci_express/src/bridge.rs
@@ -196,7 +196,7 @@ pub const fn outbound_window(
     size_bytes: u64,
 ) -> Option<[(u32, u32); 5]> {
     if index >= OUTBOUND_ENTRIES
-        || size_bytes < MINIMUM_TRANSLATION_BYTES
+        || size_bytes <= MINIMUM_TRANSLATION_BYTES
         || !size_bytes.is_power_of_two()
     {
         return None;
